                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f3d63727-24e8-3e73-a2fd-d0537b40a149",
                        "entry_id": "6bcc0553-8fda-3a57-a416-31dc1fce572a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "één kleine korrel van hagel, een bevroren regendruppel"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5ea4d7c5-2f40-4c30-b6c5-1fe8d1af222c",
                                "sense_id": "f3d63727-24e8-3e73-a2fd-d0537b40a149",
                                "text": "Dit haltervormige ijsdeeltje blijkt overigens ook voor te komen op opnamen in de toppen van onweerswolken waar met een vliegtuig doorheen werd gevlogen. De twee onderzoekers opperen dat het ontstaan van dit nieuwe ijsdeeltje een belangrijke rol zou kunnen spelen bij de vorming van de èmbryo's'van hagelkorrels in onweerswolken."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "879541ce-dde4-3b26-a9ba-69d7834e1a64",
                        "entry_id": "6bcc0553-8fda-3a57-a416-31dc1fce572a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "een van de vele kleine kogeltjes die tegelijkertijd met een hagelgeweer worden afgeschoten"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d915161a-c4b9-41e2-9ffb-1324b8e8fdca",
                                "sense_id": "879541ce-dde4-3b26-a9ba-69d7834e1a64",
                                "text": "Behalve het kapotte raam en een tiental hagelkorrels op en rond zijn bed trof de Hammenaar de nodige ínslagen'van het hagelschot op de buitengevel van zijn woning aan. \"Het is dan allemaal wel niet expres gebeurd, maar onzorgvuldig is het natuurlijk wel. Voor hetzelfde geld was het minder goed afgelopen en krijg je de volle laag. Kort van te voren stond ik namelijk nog door dat raam naar buiten te kijken.\""
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0b7721a9-ef0f-305c-93f0-e1dcf6c2343c",
                        "entry_id": "6bcc0553-8fda-3a57-a416-31dc1fce572a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "chalazion, een chronische, granulomateuze ontsteking van een kliertje in het ooglid, de klier van Meibom"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a4a1e0d6-171e-43a2-b9d3-9d6429bbe9e6",
                        "source_entry_id": "6bcc0553-8fda-3a57-a416-31dc1fce572a",
                        "source_sense_id": "f3d63727-24e8-3e73-a2fd-d0537b40a149",
                        "target_lang_word": "graupel",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "graupel",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "14536659-94c4-3b28-828e-df65a47e3afc",
                                        "entry_id": "e561842e-0aa1-39fb-b965-7032fcf79c1a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A precipitation that forms when supercooled droplets of water condense on a snowflake."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "21508fe2-15d6-4950-8954-12d102374066",
                                                "sense_id": "14536659-94c4-3b28-828e-df65a47e3afc",
                                                "text": "Is it desirable in giving the falls of hail to draw a distinction between \"graupel\" and true hail?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9a2fb913-2b31-4c12-aee2-daf6e34cd17c",
                                                "sense_id": "14536659-94c4-3b28-828e-df65a47e3afc",
                                                "text": "November.— […] Smart shower of graupel (i.e. frozen snow in pellets), with snow at 9 p.m. on 10th."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7ce379ab-0086-4c74-a3ef-479ab551e082",
                                                "sense_id": "14536659-94c4-3b28-828e-df65a47e3afc",
                                                "text": "In a paper in this month's Petermann's Mittheilungen Prof. H. Fritz treats of the Geographical Distribution of Hail. […] [B]alls of true hail hav[e] an icy structure, whereas the balls of graupel are only small pellets of snow. […] With increase in latitude and in height the fall of graupel increases and that of hail decreases, while hailstones of large size are most frequent towards the equator."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0b9e91b3-ac18-4c8d-8caf-16c03b36c5fb",
                                                "sense_id": "14536659-94c4-3b28-828e-df65a47e3afc",
                                                "text": "The steam of the horses and their breath came back in turbid clouds, and the snow, or soft hail (now known as graupel), cut white streaks through them into travellers' eyes, and danced on the roof like lozenges."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5269e807-4bed-3c70-a365-e5e0b99ce15d",
                                        "entry_id": "e561842e-0aa1-39fb-b965-7032fcf79c1a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A small ball of rime resulting from this process."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c748c692-698e-475a-a25a-c2c194d9c535",
                                                "sense_id": "5269e807-4bed-3c70-a365-e5e0b99ce15d",
                                                "text": "It is established that graupels and hailstones are cone-shaped with rounded apexes and that they become egg-shaped as a result of growth during descent."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e2f63bf3-f4d9-4d3b-9b03-613fbb3603ad",
                                                "sense_id": "5269e807-4bed-3c70-a365-e5e0b99ce15d",
                                                "text": "[W]hen an ice or snow crystal collides with supercooled droplets, the droplets will freeze on the surface of the crystal to form rime. […] [C]ontinued riming will eventually produce a particle that is completely covered by rimes such that the original crystal shape can no longer be recognized. The particle now becomes a graupel (sometimes also called a soft hail or snow pellet). […] By convention, a graupel should be smaller than 5 mm in diameter. If it becomes greater than 5 mm in diameter (2.5 mm in radius) it will be called hail."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
